<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Brandenburger Gold Coast</h1><p class="st-meta">1682 CE – 1721 CE · capital Gross Friedrichsburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Brandenburg-Prussia's short-lived colony on the Gold Coast, centred on the fort of Gross Friedrichsburg near Cape Three Points.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Elector <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-elector-of-brandenburg">Frederick William</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> chartered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-african-company">Brandenburg African Company</a> in 1682, hoping to share in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic trade</a>. An expedition under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-friedrich-von-der-groeben">Otto Friedrich von der Groeben</a> reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahanta-people">Ahanta</a> coast and in 1683 founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gross-friedrichsburg">Gross Friedrichsburg</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princes-town-ghana">Pokesu</a> (Princes Town), after treaties with local chiefs. Smaller posts followed at Takrama and at Accada, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-dorothea">Fort Dorothea</a> was built.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The colony traded guns and cloth for gold, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and slaves, many of them shipped to the Danish island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-thomas-u-s-virgin-islands">St Thomas</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>. Its garrisons were tiny and depended on alliances with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahanta-people">Ahanta</a> leaders. The company was always short of capital and ships, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> rivals from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dutch-gold-coast">Dutch Gold Coast</a> obstructed its trade.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-i-of-prussia">Frederick William I of Prussia</a>, uninterested in overseas ventures, sold the posts to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> in 1717. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahanta-people">Ahanta</a> merchant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-conny">Jan Conny</a> held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gross-friedrichsburg">Gross Friedrichsburg</a> against them until 1724. The fort, renamed Fort <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayapura">Hollandia</a>, survives as a ruin at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princes-town-ghana">Princes Town</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/brandenburger-gold-coast.jpg" alt="Brandenburger Gold Coast" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Fornax · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kriegsflagge_Kur-Brandenburgische_Flotte.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1682 CE – 1721 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gross Friedrichsburg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Otto Friedrich von der Groeben, Jan Conny</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestant Christianity, Akan traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Ahanta</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ghana">Ghana</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gross Friedrichsburg, Prussian Gold Coast</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1702&amp;focus=brandenburger-gold-coast" aria-label="Brandenburger Gold Coast on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4623 2000 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Brandenburger Gold Coast lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4943 2256L5282 625M4943 2256L5300 622M4943 2256L4965 2242"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5282 625h0M5300 622h0M4965 2242h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4943 2256h0"/><path class